{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>ובצלעי</b> — the reference is to my illness, from the root צ-ל-ע, and it is one who limps on his thigh, because he is unable to stand on his feet and walk like any healthy person." "<b>נכים</b> — an adjective on the pattern of מתים, and it means lowly in spirit, like גאים. And some say: like 'lame of feet,' corresponding to ובצלעי." "And the meaning of ולא ידעתי — that they are witnesses of violence, whom I knew and examined. In my illness they gathered; the נכים, people inferior to them, assembled to mock me. And even though I did not know who they were, they tore my flesh by way of parable — that they would speak evil against me." "<b>ולא דמו</b> — from the root ד-מ-ם, of the doubled-letter [binyan] pattern, like תמו דברי איוב."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:40.792118417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}